# Managed by homelab-postfix -- do NOT edit by hand (re-copied from
# /usr/share/homelab-postfix/nftables/ on every package configure).
#
# The postfix sender pool must make OUTBOUND connections to arbitrary
# external MX servers on tcp/25 to deliver mail off-fleet. The fleet base
# firewall's 'inet filter output' chain is `policy drop`, and the
# homelab-agent fleet-trust baseline only accepts intra-fleet destinations
# (10.50.0.0/22, 10.45.0.0/16, 10.20.0.0/16) -- external MX hosts are
# arbitrary public IPs not in that set, so without this the senders cannot
# reach any public :25. An accept living in a separate table cannot
# override another base chain's drop, so it MUST be added into this chain.
#
# Loaded two ways, both safe (same pattern as homelab-agent fleet-trust /
# homelab-node-exporter metrics):
#   * at boot via /etc/nftables.conf's `include "/etc/nftables.d/*"`,
#     inside that file's single atomic `flush ruleset` load;
#   * live on package configure via `nft -f` of just this file (a bare
#     `add rule`, no `flush`) -- so the bad-ips dynamic set (runtime
#     state, not on disk) is never lost. The postinst deletes any prior
#     rule carrying the comment below before re-applying, so a live
#     re-apply never stacks duplicates.
add rule inet filter output tcp dport 25 accept comment "homelab-postfix-smtp-egress"
